Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-05-01
Subject: Use System.ParamStr while reading bootstrap compiler options
License: expat

FPC 2.6.0 reads command-line options through `objpas.ParamStr`, which
returns an AnsiString and normally comes from the RTL ObjPas unit.  The
bootstrap compiler does not need the ObjPas unit for option scanning, and
FPC 2.4.0 used `System.ParamStr` at the same call site.

Use `System.ParamStr` so the translated bootstrap compiler does not need
to resolve the ObjPas RTL unit just to read its command-line arguments.

--- a/compiler/options.pas
+++ b/compiler/options.pas
@@ -2081,7 +2081,7 @@ begin
    begin
      inc(paramindex);
-     opts:=objpas.paramstr(paramindex);
+     opts:=system.paramstr(paramindex);
      case opts[1] of
        '@' :
          if not firstpass then
